                            <comment id="16737790" author="q79969786" created="Wed, 9 Jan 2019 02:53:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;cc &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=gszadovszky&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;gszadovszky&quot;&gt;gszadovszky&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16738074" author="gszadovszky" created="Wed, 9 Jan 2019 10:27:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yumwang&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yumwang&quot;&gt;yumwang&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-column/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/filter2/predicate/UserDefinedPredicate.java#L47&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;UserDefinedPredicate.keep(T)&lt;/a&gt; shall handle &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; values because the parquet-mr library do invokes it with a &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;. This is the only way the filtering API can check if a &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; value fulfills the UDP.&lt;br/&gt;
It did not occur before the ColumnIndex feature because the statistics and the dictionary filters invokes &lt;tt&gt;keep(T)&lt;/tt&gt; only in some special scenarios (e.g. &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/filter2/statisticslevel/StatisticsFilter.java#L385&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;if all the values are &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; in the column chunk&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;br/&gt;
So the problem is at the client side. Please, update your code so that &lt;tt&gt;keep(T)&lt;/tt&gt; checks for &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; value and returns accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is another issue that the described behavior is not properly documented. I&apos;ll create a JIRA about it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Closing this issue as not a bug.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16738424" author="q79969786" created="Wed, 9 Jan 2019 16:45:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=gszadovszky&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;gszadovszky&quot;&gt;gszadovszky&lt;/a&gt; Thanks a lot.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16884204" author="rdblue" created="Fri, 12 Jul 2019 22:17:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;We discussed this on &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SPARK-28371&quot; title=&quot;Parquet &amp;quot;starts with&amp;quot; filter is not null-safe&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;SPARK-28371&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;SPARK-28371&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Previously, Parquet did not&#160;fail if a UserDefinedPredicate did not&#160;handle null values, so I think that it is a regression that Parquet will cause previously working code to fail. I think that it is correct for Parquet to call a UDP the way that it is, but that Parquet should catch exceptions thrown by the predicate and&#160;should process the row group where there error was thrown. That way, Parquet can keep the optimization for columns that are all null, but it doesn&apos;t break existing code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yumwang&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yumwang&quot;&gt;yumwang&lt;/a&gt;, would you like to submit a PR for this?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16885138" author="gszadovszky" created="Mon, 15 Jul 2019 12:05:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=rdblue&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;rdblue&quot;&gt;rdblue&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
Previously, parquet might fail in special cases for both &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/filter2/dictionarylevel/DictionaryFilter.java#L393&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;dictionary&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/master/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/filter2/statisticslevel/StatisticsFilter.java#L369&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;statistics&lt;/a&gt; filters. However, because of performance reasons, column indexes invokes it all the time. I agree, it is a regression and my previous &quot;fix&quot; of having it properly documented was not enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=yumwang&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;yumwang&quot;&gt;yumwang&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;m happy to help you with this or work on it if you don&apos;t have the time.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16885201" author="q79969786" created="Mon, 15 Jul 2019 12:56:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=gszadovszky&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;gszadovszky&quot;&gt;gszadovszky&lt;/a&gt; Please work on this.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
